+## 19. Quick Picks Redesign and Taste-Based Ranking (patch quickpicks)
+
+- UI: Quick picks now looks like YouTube Music. Larger title, an outlined "Play all" button (it now really plays all the picks as a queue), pages of 4 songs where the next page peeks from the right edge, and no page dots.
+- Algorithm: new `QuickPicksRanker`. Candidates are the related songs from the local database (plus the most played songs when the library is small). Each song gets a score from: how related it is to recent listening, how much you play and follow its artists (last 60 days), a small bonus for liked songs, a penalty for songs played in the last 10 plays or played to death, and a small random part so the list changes on refresh. At most 2 songs per artist.
+
+### Modified Files
+- `ui/screens/HomeScreenComponents.kt`, `viewmodels/HomeViewModel.kt`
+- New: `utils/QuickPicksRanker.kt`
+
+
 ---
 
 **Overall Summary**: Removed crash-prone null assertions across the app and InnerTube, added selection UI for queuing and playlist management, fixed selection state resets on data refresh, and restored the mood/category chip suggestions on the home screen. Also made the app open much faster (first frame about 357ms on release) and cut the song start delay from 2-5 seconds of URL resolving to about 0.45 seconds, by remembering the working stream client, warming up the JS player, and prefetching the next song.
